Also, some comments are outdated, incomplete, or missing.

Some comments on the fields in `queueSet` reference a now-non-existent field `config`.

```
// queue is an array of requests with additional metadata required for
// the FQScheduler
```
.. reads a bit odd, there is no "array" in sight.

`queue::index` has no comment.

```
// Note that the FIFO list is not safe for concurrent use by multiple
// goroutines without additional locking or coordination.
```
The presence of "without ..." suggests that it is adding information, but as far as I can tell it is not.

```
	// Enqueue enqueues the specified request into the list and
	// returns a removeFromFIFOFunc function that can be used to remove the
	// request from the list
	Enqueue(*request) removeFromFIFOFunc
```
I would feel more comfortable with an explicit statement about concurrency and that returned `removeFromFIFOFunc`.  Perhaps something like updating the comment on `fifo` to say something like the following.
```
// Note that a FIFO, including the removeFromFIFOFuncs returned from Enqueue,
// is not safe for concurrent use by multiple goroutines.
```

```
// promiseFactory returns a WriteOnce
// - whose Set method is invoked with the queueSet locked, and
// - whose Get method is invoked with the queueSet not locked.
type promiseFactory func(initial interface{}, doneCh <-chan struct{}, doneVal interface{}) promise.WriteOnce
```
.. should also describe the significance of the parameters.  Since it is the same as for `promise.NewWriteOnce`, a reference to that would suffice.

Checking that locking discipline is followed would be easier if each non-Locked method of queueSet had a comment that explicitly says whether the method is lock-oblivious or an entry method.  This would make it a local check to avoid the case of an entry method calling another entry method (which would cause a deadlock, not the symptom in this Issue).

The function comment on `queueSet::setConfiguration` uses the wrong capitalization for the function name.

```
// lockAndSyncTime acquires the lock and updates the virtual time.
// Doing them together avoids the mistake of modify some queue state ...
```
s/modify/modifying/
